It should help with any refresh rate higher than 60Hz.
To temper expectations a bit: this fix will not increase frame rates in any situation - if a computer can't handle 60 frames, then rendering on each of those makes sense. But it should reduce resource consumption on machines that can handle way more than 60.

Yea, it looks to me like another high-Hz oversight in the core scripts.
