You are correct that MZ use's Pixi's ticker, whereas MV implements its own ticker using requestAnimationFrame. However, Pixi's ticker is also driven by requestAnimationFrame, and (to my understanding) both implementations will generally match the ticks to the display's refresh rate.
Here is the relevant function in MZ:
JavaScript:
Graphics._onTick = function(deltaTime) {
    this._fpsCounter.startTick();
    if (this._tickHandler) {
        this._tickHandler(deltaTime); // Graphics._tickHandler holds a reference to SceneManager.update
    }
    if (this._canRender()) {
        this._app.render();
    }
    this._fpsCounter.endTick();
};
This function calls SceneManager.update, which then uses deltaTime (the time elapsed since the last frame) to call SceneManager.updateMain approximately 60 times per second. But as you can see, the render function is called outside of that--every tick.

